{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["And the reason for <b>in the hearing of all who enter my city</b> — that is to say, the entire people are here, and they are the ones who know and are witnesses. Do not worry about denial or retraction, but bury your dead there from now on, for it is yours and I cannot take it back. But Abraham did not do so, for even after he weighed out the silver, he first took possession of the field and the cave and established them under his authority in the presence of the townspeople and all who came to the city gate — the merchants and the foreign residents who were present there — and only afterward did he bury her."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:33:25.260223702Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}